{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-eviction-terminal-only-row-survives",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 12 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 9/L9): with LOHRA_MAX_SUBSESSIONS=2, spawning a third child once the registry is already at cap (two terminal children) evicts the OLDEST terminal entry to make room — a subsequent collect_session against the evicted sub_id returns 'no sub-session <id>', proving it was actually removed from the registry, not merely full. Deterministic and race-free: each spawn is followed by a collect_session(wait:true) before the next spawn, so every prior child is definitely terminal (not running) by the time the next one is spawned — eviction only ever removes a terminal entry (decision 9), so this ordering makes the outcome unambiguous.",
  "argv": [
    "chat",
    "SCEN:parent spawn three children over a cap of two",
    "--json",
    "--provider",
    "ollama",
    "--model",
    "stub-coder:1b"
